rank2-contact-release-lemma.statement:
On a fixed positive all-double normal-fan stratum, suppose an endpoint
chamber arc contains a deletable unmarked vertex.  Prove that there is
a simultaneous piecewise-rational motion of \(A_0,A_2,K\) which:

1. preserves every exact \(P,Q,R\) chamber area and all three crossings;
2. satisfies every active common-plane support-contact inequality;
3. retains each zero-coordinate boundary endpoint exactly;
4. does not decrease the zero-charge capacity; and
5. continues until a vertex deletion or a declared boundary event.

If no such motion exists, derive the exact Farkas-dual
common-plane inequality certifying infeasibility.

triangle-boundary-generic-perturbation.statement:
Assume the surviving transformed triangular (N=3) system and incidence orbit of accepted facts `09393c6edf1fc4e2`, `f8e871d10dac1791`, and `89f1aef98e9b8915`, with (t\le1/2). Suppose at least one entry of the middle vertex matrix (L) is zero and all three strict low-row inequalities hold. Prove that there are arbitrarily small perturbations (L_\varepsilon,\sigma_\varepsilon), with (U,V,A,B,t) fixed, such that:

1. all nine entries of (L_\varepsilon) are nonzero and (det L_\varepsilon\ne0);
2. column sums, midpoint compatibility, (q>1), and the incidence orbit are preserved;
3. all three row masses remain strictly below (t).

Conclude from accepted fact `89f1aef98e9b8915` that every boundary counterexample is a limit of strict systems in the sole contained-support open chamber. Do not claim that the contained-support chamber itself is excluded.
